1
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:03,630
♪

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:08,130
[RIGHT]
On the day of the equinox,

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:10,970
a twin boy and girl
will be born,

4
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:15,560
dividing the sunrise,
destined to command the daemons.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,560
[LEFT] So is said
in that eastern village.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,650
And these twins will
not only sunder night and day,

7
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:23,730
-but the whole world.
-[infants crying]

8
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:28,070
[RIGHT] Some 400 years ago,

9
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:31,200
a great war tore
the nation in twain,

10
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:34,450
with those who wield daemons
pulling the strings.

11
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:37,200
The people of Higashi tried

12
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,750
to keep the twins
inside their village,

13
00:00:39,790 --> 00:00:42,420
hoping to make use
of their powers.

14
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:44,960
Their parents realized

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,920
the children were in danger
as things stood,

16
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:50,470
so they made plans
to flee the village.

17
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:52,970
But try though as they might,

18
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:55,560
they only managed
to escape with Asa.

19
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:59,850
The twins have powers
that are their right to claim.

20
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:02,020
Break and Seal.

21
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:06,270
One, the ability
to forcibly unravel all things.

22
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,280
That is the power of Break.

23
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,450
[LEFT] The other, the ability
to forcibly close all things.

24
00:01:13,490 --> 00:01:14,910
That is Seal.

25
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,200
[ASA] If I had any choice,

26
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:20,750
I wouldn't be a twin fated
to fulfill some prophecy.

27
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:23,540
But now, I can choose.

28
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:27,170
And I'll get my own hands dirty.

29
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,420
[RIGHT] After she gained
the power of Break,

30
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:33,510
Asa attacked the village
to take back her brother.

31
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,550
Get away from her!

32
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:39,810
[LEFT] Amidst the chaos,

33
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:43,520
we were awoken
from our 400-year slumber.

34
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:45,190
[RIGHT] And luckily,
our new boss

35
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:46,980
is the hands-off type.

36
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:48,320
[DERA] Yuru...

37
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:51,070
these are your daemons.

38
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,450
[RIGHT] Asa is being sheltered

39
00:01:54,490 --> 00:01:57,120
by a group known
as the Kagemoris.

40
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,160
[LEFT] A subsect of Higashi,

41
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,910
who split over irreconcilable
differences.

42
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,790
[RIGHT] Yuru was offered
a place with their clan,

43
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:06,920
but chose to search
for his parents

44
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,170
without their help.

45
00:02:08,290 --> 00:02:10,670
[YURU] I'm not gonna live
my life on the run!

46
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:12,880
And I have got
no reason to hide!

47
00:02:12,930 --> 00:02:16,550
I don't care if you're from
Higashi or the Kagemoris.

48
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:17,890
I'm not afraid.

49
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:20,140
If you want my head,
come and get it!

50
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:22,100
[LEFT] And by appearances,

51
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:24,730
even their own clan
isn't a monolith.

52
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,020
[ASA] The truth is...

53
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,560
I died once.

54
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:31,860
[GONZO] Humanity is better off
without Break or Seal.

55
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:34,280
They are too great a threat.

56
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,910
And since we share their blood,

57
00:02:35,950 --> 00:02:37,780
it's our responsibility
to make sure

58
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:39,450
they're taken care of.

59
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:42,250
The village that produces
Break and Seal

60
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:43,750
should be allowed to live on.

61
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:46,960
We mustn't reject
their very existence.

62
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,960
[RIGHT]
And it seems other forces

63
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,500
are throwing themselves
into the fray.

64
00:02:51,550 --> 00:02:53,800
We must tread carefully.

65
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:04,020
[♪ opening theme song playing]

66
00:04:31,690 --> 00:04:34,570
[MAN] Yes, sir.
I followed him partway up.

67
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:36,240
Only as far as you said.

68
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,950
Yes, by my estimation
the "shaman"

69
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:40,450
should be inside by now.

70
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:42,570
[SHINGO] Good. Well done.

71
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:45,870
I just needed to know
when he arrived in the village.

72
00:04:45,910 --> 00:04:47,870
Wait there for further orders.

73
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,960
Hey, Ivan...

74
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,830
-You're up.
-[Ivan exhales]

75
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,590
[IVAN] Aye-aye, sir.

76
00:04:55,090 --> 00:04:56,380
Time to get to it, Shokyo.

77
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,010
[SHOKYO] Excuse me?

78
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,630
You mean, "Please aid me,
Master Shokyo!"

79
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:04,510
Come on, tell me who's
the master of who again here?

80
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:06,010
[SHOKYO] Silence, monkey!

81
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:07,890
I'll fillet you like a fish!

82
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:11,390
[IVAN] Daikyo, talk some sense
into your other half.

83
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:12,810
[DAIKYO] Mm...

84
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:14,900
[IVAN] Look at me
when I talk to you.

85
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:17,190
You two sure like
acting high and mighty

86
00:05:17,230 --> 00:05:18,280
for a couple of daemons

87
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:20,070
who aren't even able to move
without a master.

88
00:05:20,110 --> 00:05:21,490
[SHOKYO] The insolence!

89
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:23,490
Your simian brain
could do nothing

90
00:05:23,530 --> 00:05:24,950
if it weren't for our help!

91
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:26,950
Who do you think's putting food
on your table?

92
00:05:26,990 --> 00:05:28,750
That's me, you lazybones.

93
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:30,040
I thought you were sharp.

94
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,830
-[SHOKYO] Screw you, baboon!
-[SHINGO] Shut up!

95
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:33,000
Get a move on!

96
00:05:33,370 --> 00:05:36,300
I'm not payin' you a fortune
so you can talk my ear off!

97
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:37,550
[IVAN] Yeah, yeah.

98
00:05:46,510 --> 00:05:48,060
In we go.

99
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:52,520
This shouldn't take me
terribly long.

100
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,320
Man, that's creepy.

101
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:07,120
[birds chirping]

102
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:17,460
[KEN] Hmm. So, does this look
any better?

103
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,340
-A ton!
-[HANA] What's up?

104
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,090
Are you making weapons again?

105
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:23,380
[YURU] Uh, yeah.

106
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:24,930
[DERA] All right!

107
00:06:24,970 --> 00:06:27,010
Then I'd better give you
something to do.

108
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:29,140
What's this metal board?

109
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,470
[DERA] The old tube.

110
00:06:30,510 --> 00:06:31,730
It's square.

111
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:32,850
[beeps]

112
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:34,690
And looking at the south end...

113
00:06:34,730 --> 00:06:35,770
[Yuru exclaims]

114
00:06:35,810 --> 00:06:37,270
-[RIGHT] Whoa!
-[LEFT] Mm.

115
00:06:37,310 --> 00:06:39,730
-...nothing but scattered...
-[Yuru exclaims]

116
00:06:39,770 --> 00:06:42,030
Some are concerned we may see
a water shortage

117
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:43,860
in the western part
of the country.

118
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,370
Next, we have
the national forecast.

119
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:47,620
In Okinawa,

120
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:50,240
we expect to see
clear blue skies...

121
00:06:50,290 --> 00:06:52,870
Oh, yeah. I can't visit
the place my mother's from.

122
00:06:52,910 --> 00:06:54,080
...make sure
you pack some shorts...

123
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,080
What about you?

124
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,540
You mean me?

125
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,460
The place you said
you two were from.

126
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:59,840
Ethio... something?

127
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:03,340
[chuckles] You mean Ethiopia.
It's in Africa.

128
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:04,420
[RIGHT] Mm?

129
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:05,930
[YURU] Don't you wanna go
visit sometimes?

130
00:07:06,550 --> 00:07:07,970
Eh...

131
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:10,760
it's pretty ridiculously
far away.

132
00:07:10,850 --> 00:07:12,060
I could, though.

133
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:14,890
And I shouldn't take that
for granted, now should I?

134
00:07:15,230 --> 00:07:18,440
There's no way I could go back
to Higashi Village now.

135
00:07:18,770 --> 00:07:20,150
It's not safe.

136
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,520
[birds chirping]

137
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:23,820
[bird screeching]

138
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:26,610
[YURU] But I left so much
behind back there.

139
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:29,120
I wish I could see it again.

140
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,700
[Yama yelps]

141
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:36,370
[YAMA] No! What's going on here?

142
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:37,670
Hey, shaman.

143
00:07:37,710 --> 00:07:38,670
[Yama yelps]

144
00:07:38,710 --> 00:07:40,290
You wait right there.

145
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:41,880
Be back in a jiff.

146
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,210
[SHOKYO] Oi, monkey.

147
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:46,670
I can sense them.
There are daemons in the keep.

148
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:49,510
All the way up there, huh?

149
00:07:49,550 --> 00:07:50,970
There's a saying about fools

150
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:53,140
and something
liking high places.

151
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,980
[SHOKYO] It's fools and monkeys.

152
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:56,810
[IVAN] It's fools
and smoke, you fool.

153
00:07:56,850 --> 00:07:59,190
[SHOKYO]
You dare call me a fool, fool?

154
00:07:59,690 --> 00:08:01,060
[exhales]

155
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:02,860
♪

156
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:06,940
[breathes uneasily]

157
00:08:07,450 --> 00:08:08,650
[man laughs]

158
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:10,490
That's pretty rough, buddy.

159
00:08:10,530 --> 00:08:11,870
Yeah, you're tellin' me.

160
00:08:11,910 --> 00:08:13,030
[BOTH] Hm?

161
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,500
-[MAN 1] You know that guy?
-[MAN 2] Nope.

162
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:22,710
What's your name?

163
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:25,050
-How'd you get in here?
-[clanging]

164
00:08:25,090 --> 00:08:26,260
-[MAN 2] Hey...
-[both grunt]

165
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:30,630
No daemons.

166
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,850
[man whimpers]

167
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,680
[screams]

168
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:36,980
How annoying.

169
00:08:45,070 --> 00:08:46,190
[slashing]

170
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,650
[man grunting]

171
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,030
-[slashing]
-[man groans]

172
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:52,200
[thuds]

173
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:54,200
Not him either.

174
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:59,500
[men yelling]

175
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,620
-[IVAN] Nope. Nada.
-[men grunting]

176
00:09:01,670 --> 00:09:04,130
[IVAN] Bzz... None of them.

177
00:09:04,170 --> 00:09:05,960
Not even one.

178
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:08,590
[sword slashing]

179
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,090
[Ivan gasps]

180
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:11,430
[grunting]

181
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:16,970
That was quite a greeting.

182
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:18,640
[all gasp]

183
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,060
Who are you?

184
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,440
Are you with those raiders
from the last time?

185
00:09:23,810 --> 00:09:26,980
We have people watching
every possible entrance.

186
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:28,440
How'd you get inside?

187
00:09:28,490 --> 00:09:30,280
And without even
breaking the barrier!

188
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:32,860
[men grunting]

189
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:35,200
[Yamaha gasps]

190
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,500
Look at you.

191
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:49,130
I heard about some daemon
they had bound in a cage.

192
00:09:49,170 --> 00:09:51,260
-You look like Asa.
-[grunts]

193
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:53,630
You let me cut straight
through those guys,

194
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:55,260
but came to save the old lady?

195
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,260
[Yamaha grunts]

196
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:58,560
I suppose that means
she's your master.

197
00:10:00,430 --> 00:10:01,680
[Ivan gasps]

198
00:10:06,650 --> 00:10:08,270
Didn't miss a beat attacking me!

199
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,320
You realize
I've got your master?

200
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:12,490
If she's a daemon,

201
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:15,120
her other half must be nearby.

202
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:19,580
But where? Stay on guard!

203
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:21,500
[SHOKYO] Uh? Look down, monkey!

204
00:10:22,370 --> 00:10:23,500
[Ivan grunts]

205
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,590
[gasps]

206
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:32,880
[Asa (fake) sighs]

207
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:37,180
Why you gotta do me like that,
Shokyo? Good grief.

208
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:38,350
[SHOKYO] What?

209
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,930
You're saying that one leg
was worth more than your life?

210
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:43,560
You should be kneeling
on your hands and knees

211
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:44,770
thanking your savior!

212
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:48,060
And how do you expect me
to kneel on this leg? Hm?

213
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,650
So you're the fake Asa?

214
00:10:51,110 --> 00:10:53,070
But you're made
to look a lot more childlike

215
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:54,490
than the real deal.

216
00:10:55,450 --> 00:10:57,820
You throw this cute
and defenseless little burden

217
00:10:57,870 --> 00:10:58,870
at that big brother,

218
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,120
and there's no chance
he'd ever wanna run away.

219
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,120
Messed up, if you ask me.

220
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,790
And not one of these villagers
could see daemons.

221
00:11:06,830 --> 00:11:08,500
Did she keep it like that
on purpose?

222
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,340
Hoard all the power,
so these poor chumps

223
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:12,420
have no choice
but to worship her?

224
00:11:12,710 --> 00:11:14,840
Your master's
not just messed up.

225
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,630
She's downright repulsive.

226
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,800
Anyway, guess
I can't kill your master,

227
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:21,890
'cause then you'd become
a stray.

228
00:11:21,930 --> 00:11:23,810
It's that face I want,

229
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:26,640
so I won't have you going back
to your original form.

230
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:29,480
I could contract you myself.

231
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:32,530
But my pair, Magatsuhi,
just wouldn't like that.

232
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:36,780
More specifically, Shokyo here's
incompatible with everyone.

233
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:38,110
Worst case,

234
00:11:38,410 --> 00:11:40,780
short stuff might straight up
kill you just for fun.

235
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,580
[SHOKYO] Oh, I'd kill her.

236
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,870
Well, you heard the sword.

237
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:47,460
Now if you come quietly
without complaining,

238
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:50,210
I'll do you a solid
and spare your master's life.

239
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,960
So hop to it, you phony.

240
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:55,590
Down there?

241
00:11:55,630 --> 00:11:58,130
Off the mountain.
It'll be fun.

242
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:00,260
Uh?

243
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:02,140
♪

244
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:07,180
[sighs]

245
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:12,940
[Asa (fake) grunts]

246
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:14,530
[ASA (FAKE)] You win.

247
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:16,440
-I'll go.
-[Yamaha gasps]

248
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,280
[sighs]

249
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,280
[footsteps]

250
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:31,080
[IVAN] The other half
of this pair never wound up

251
00:12:31,130 --> 00:12:32,750
making their grand entrance.

252
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:34,460
I wonder why.

253
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,920
Are they up to something?

254
00:12:37,170 --> 00:12:40,220
I'd like a human hostage
for insurance, too.

255
00:12:40,470 --> 00:12:42,640
[all crying]

256
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,970
[screaming]

257
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:46,560
[Azami whimpers]

258
00:12:48,230 --> 00:12:50,270
Now there's a child
who won't struggle!

259
00:12:50,310 --> 00:12:51,850
[boy crying]

260
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:56,280
[boy crying] Mommy!
Please, get up!

261
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:58,570
-Not again.
-Awful.

262
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:02,280
Our little village might not
bounce back from this attack.

263
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,160
[grunts] We need
to get away now!

264
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,530
The monster's still here!

265
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,410
Danji, remember
you used to tell me

266
00:13:07,450 --> 00:13:10,000
you'd like to see
the world outside with Yuru?

267
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,670
[gasps] Yeah?

268
00:13:11,710 --> 00:13:13,130
It's time now.

269
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:15,460
You're going down there.
By yourself.

270
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,170
Wait, you don't mean...

271
00:13:17,210 --> 00:13:18,920
You can't, Ma! What about you?

272
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:20,970
I am staying in the village.

273
00:13:21,010 --> 00:13:22,680
You boys might come home
one day.

274
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:25,140
You'll need someone to welcome
you back with open arms,

275
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,430
and that's me.

276
00:13:26,470 --> 00:13:27,970
But Mama...

277
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:31,350
Here, I wrote you directions
to help get down the mountain.

278
00:13:31,690 --> 00:13:33,150
Follow each one to a tee.

279
00:13:33,190 --> 00:13:34,730
[Danji breathes shakily]

280
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:38,360
I'm going to be fine.

281
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,530
Yuru needs you,
so get outta here.

282
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,400
And if you do see
Mine and Nagisa,

283
00:13:42,450 --> 00:13:44,530
give them my regards.

284
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:48,410
[Yama grunting]

285
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,210
Who was that?

286
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,710
What's he after?

287
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:56,710
I want no part
of whatever's happening here!

288
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:58,590
[both chirping]

289
00:13:58,630 --> 00:13:59,800
[Yama grunts]

290
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,880
[Tsugais shrieking]

291
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,010
[Yama gasps]

292
00:14:03,470 --> 00:14:06,100
I believe I said you were
to wait right where I left you.

293
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:07,970
[Yama whimpers]

294
00:14:09,010 --> 00:14:10,100
[Yama grunts]

295
00:14:12,730 --> 00:14:14,230
[Azami whimpers]

296
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,940
[Yama grunts]

297
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:23,200
You two go ahead without me.

298
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:30,950
[both whimpering]

299
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:33,290
[Asa (Fake) gasps]

300
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:38,420
Welcome to the outside world.

301
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:40,090
[Azami whimpers]

302
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:43,420
[Tsugais growl]

303
00:14:43,470 --> 00:14:44,970
[Yama whimpers]

304
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:50,310
Well, I didn't have
another exit route planned out.

305
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:52,770
-[Yama gasps]
-[both shriek]

306
00:14:52,810 --> 00:14:56,270
Too bad. Looks like
I need myself a guide.

307
00:14:56,310 --> 00:14:59,400
Maybe a kind shaman
could help me.

308
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:00,900
What do you say?

309
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:06,870
[Danji panting, grunting]

310
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,720
[Danji grunts]

311
00:15:32,770 --> 00:15:34,060
[wings fluttering]

312
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:35,390
[Danji groans]

313
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,940
[DANJI] Am I outside?

314
00:15:42,070 --> 00:15:43,480
Yuru!

315
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:45,450
Where's Yuru?

316
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,780
He needs me!

317
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,410
[gasps]

318
00:15:49,910 --> 00:15:51,410
[horse neighs]

319
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:56,870
Hello! Want a lift?

320
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:03,210
[DANJI] Wait.
You know the Divine Guardians?

321
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:04,550
[OSHIRASAMA] That's right.

322
00:16:04,590 --> 00:16:07,050
We have been friends
a long time.

323
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:09,380
In fact, I came across them
fleeing the village

324
00:16:09,430 --> 00:16:11,140
with the boy twin
just the other day!

325
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:13,050
Boy twin? That's Yuru!

326
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:16,060
They said they would hide
inside a busy human town.

327
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,520
They were riding in a car.

328
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,850
A what now?

329
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:21,270
[Danji gasps] Huh?

330
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:25,190
[OSHIRASAMA] Yes! One of those!

331
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:27,240
[DANJI] Good.

332
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:29,450
Yuru made it
down the mountain safely.

333
00:16:29,490 --> 00:16:30,660
Thank all the gods.

334
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:33,740
But I still don't know
where I can find him.

335
00:16:33,780 --> 00:16:35,790
Hmm, let me see.

336
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:39,000
The license plate on their car
was registered to the capital.

337
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:41,250
It may be best to search there!

338
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:43,130
-Shall we?
-Uh, what?

339
00:16:43,170 --> 00:16:45,920
How exciting!
I've never been to the capital!

340
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,590
Oh, first things first!

341
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:50,010
I had best tell my master
before we go!

342
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:52,510
May we stop by my home first?

343
00:16:52,550 --> 00:16:54,640
[DANJI] Uh, yeah, sure.

344
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:57,010
[horse neighs]

345
00:16:58,310 --> 00:16:59,890
[OSHIRASAMA'S MASTER]
How nice!

346
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:02,940
You're taking a trip to see
some friends who live far away?

347
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,400
And I have company!

348
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,900
My friend's master's friend
is here, too!

349
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,360
[DANJI] Hello, ma'am! Uh?

350
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,990
[chuckles]

351
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,320
My, oh, my...

352
00:17:12,370 --> 00:17:14,450
What a charming young man
you've found.

353
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:16,410
Please do take care now.

354
00:17:16,450 --> 00:17:18,160
[horse neighs]

355
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:21,830
[OSHIRASAMA'S MASTER]
Watch out for cars on the road.

356
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:24,290
Be careful not to scare
ordinary folks!

357
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:26,210
Right. I'll see you later.

358
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:29,420
And remember to actually enjoy
your time in the city!

359
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:30,920
[OSHIRASAMA] May I really?

360
00:17:30,970 --> 00:17:32,800
-Ooh! Yippee!
-[horse neighs]

361
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:35,930
Okay! Let's get
the highway experience!

362
00:17:35,970 --> 00:17:37,100
What?

363
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:39,390
The highway?

364
00:17:39,430 --> 00:17:40,730
[OSHIRASAMA] Mm-hmm.

365
00:17:41,430 --> 00:17:43,400
[Danji screaming]

366
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:45,360
[OSHIRASAMA] Yay!

367
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,780
-[Oshirasama laughing]
-[Danji screaming]

368
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:49,900
Shall we stop by the rest area?

369
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,570
[Danji continues screaming]

370
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,170
[mobile phone chirps]

371
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:12,260
All right. What have we here?

372
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:13,930
[grunts]

373
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,470
Dera, heads up.

374
00:18:16,510 --> 00:18:18,180
I've got some
extra work tonight.

375
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:20,430
Sure. Take it easy out there.

376
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:23,440
And you should know,
the shaman was killed.

377
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,820
[DERA] Hmm.

378
00:18:31,990 --> 00:18:33,280
[BANDIT] By the time
we got to his shop,

379
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,150
it was already too late.

380
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:37,200
The shaman was long dead.

381
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,700
Ooh, boy, what a casket.

382
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:41,950
Something this size
won't be easy to bury.

383
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,790
I hope you know I'm gonna have
to charge you extra for this.

384
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:45,880
Oh, yeah.

385
00:18:46,290 --> 00:18:48,290
Didn't the shaman have
a couple of daemons of his own?

386
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:50,550
Are they stuck somewhere
as strays?

387
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:54,050
[BANDIT] Oh, you mean
Lady and Gentleman.

388
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:55,720
[birds chirping]

389
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:01,810
[BANDIT] We found them chopped
in half right beside him.

390
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:03,600
[HANA] That's terrible.

391
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:06,140
Poor little guys
weren't even fighters.

392
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:08,820
Do you happen
to have their relics?

393
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:10,150
I'll bury them with him.

394
00:19:11,070 --> 00:19:12,570
Will it cost us extra?

395
00:19:13,570 --> 00:19:15,400
Nah, this one's on the house.

396
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:20,910
Anyway, one thing
before you bury him...

397
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:27,630
[Hana grunts]

398
00:19:28,670 --> 00:19:33,210
[HANA] "Dear Yuru, I have your
fake sister and a village child.

399
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:36,340
On the next full moon
at the hour of the Boar,

400
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:39,140
come to
Fujimurayama warehouse one."

401
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,220
Did the Kagemoris do this?

402
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:42,430
No clue.

403
00:19:42,470 --> 00:19:44,430
We heard from him.
Got a couple of texts

404
00:19:44,470 --> 00:19:46,480
just before he made
his trip to Higashi.

405
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:48,900
He said that Tadera
was keeping Yuru down here

406
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:50,480
after they ran away
from the village.

407
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:53,820
We had also heard the Kagemoris
made contact with him.

408
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:56,700
I don't suppose you know
where this secret hideaway is?

409
00:19:57,110 --> 00:19:59,490
Who, me? Just what do you think?

410
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:01,740
Dera called me
as his getaway driver,

411
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:03,290
and after I picked up those two,

412
00:20:03,330 --> 00:20:05,120
I dropped 'em off
at the usual safehouse.

413
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:08,460
Didn't tell me jack about
where he was going after that.

414
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,710
You know how he likes
to keep to himself.

415
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,840
Hmm, checks out.

416
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:15,460
Oh, well. There's nothing else
you can do.

417
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:18,630
That said,
if you see Dera or Yuru,

418
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,390
don't give them this message.

419
00:20:20,430 --> 00:20:22,720
Us "bandits" are gonna scope
the place out.

420
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:25,470
Whoever did this
can't find Yuru.

421
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:26,810
No matter what.

422
00:20:32,190 --> 00:20:33,650
[HANA] That's just my luck.

423
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:36,530
This job keeps bein'
a pain in my ass.

424
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,570
[DANJI] Oshirasama!

425
00:20:39,610 --> 00:20:41,740
I'm begging you!
Please, please, please!

426
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:45,370
Please, let me down!
Let me down! [cries]

427
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:51,500
Don't tell me you're scared
of heights, Danji!

428
00:20:51,540 --> 00:20:54,210
This is too much!
The capital is too much! [cries]

429
00:20:54,250 --> 00:20:56,090
Hang on a little longer!

430
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:58,590
I'm trying to find
Left and Right for you.

431
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:03,050
Their presence is so much
more powerful than most.

432
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:06,060
They should be quite easy
to track from way up here.

433
00:21:06,810 --> 00:21:08,390
Oh, wow!

434
00:21:08,430 --> 00:21:10,310
I know we have
plenty back home.

435
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:11,480
[Danji gasps]

436
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:16,320
[OSHIRASAMA] But the capital
is just swarming with daemons,

437
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:17,610
isn't it?

438
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,780
[bird screeching]

439
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:23,200
♪

440
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:34,840
[Hana sighs]

441
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,670
[BANDIT] That said,
if you see Dera or Yuru,

442
00:21:39,710 --> 00:21:41,720
don't give them this message.

443
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:44,340
Yeah, yeah. Don't gotta tell me.

444
00:21:44,390 --> 00:21:47,180
I'd like a peaceful life,
thank you very much.

445
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:48,390
[sighs]

446
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:53,390
Fools and smoke rise
to high places, as they say.

447
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:57,440
[♪ closing theme song playing]

448
00:23:27,870 --> 00:23:29,700
[DERA] So, who do you think
killed him?

449
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:31,990
[RIGHT] There be daemons nearby.

450
00:23:32,330 --> 00:23:34,330
[YURU] We'll take care
of this here.

451
00:23:34,370 --> 00:23:36,960
[HANA] There were some words
carved into the shaman's body.
